.TH UPDATE-CA-TRUST 8 "2026-09-16" "InterGenOS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
update-ca-trust \- regenerate system TLS certificate outputs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B update-ca-trust
.RI [ extract ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Regenerate the TLS certificate bundle and hashed certificate directory from
p11-kit's configured trust anchors in /etc/pki/anchors.
This is the InterGenOS compatibility wrapper, not the Fedora implementation.
It invokes trust extract-compat using the absolute system program path.
Both accepted forms perform the same operation and require root.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B extract
Regenerate the TLS outputs. With no arguments, perform the same operation.
Other arguments, including check, are rejected with usage and status 2.
.SH OPERATION
The compatibility helper extracts server-authentication CA anchors into a
private staging directory, checks both certificate sets, and exchanges the
complete certificate directory atomically. Extraction diagnostics, empty
output, mismatched outputs and publication failures return nonzero.
Unfamiliar existing entries in the certificate directory are refused; move
or account for them explicitly before regeneration.
.PP
An unchanged certificate set with identical output bytes and metadata requires
no publication. After a changed generation, the previous directory remains
at the printed private staging path. Inspect the new store before removing
that retained directory. Failed or interrupted publication may also retain
staging for inspection; there is no copy-based publication fallback.
.PP
The helper does not download certificates, change the anchor inputs, or
regenerate Java, email or code-signing stores. TLS PEM outputs express
certificate exclusion; they do not carry all p11-kit trust-policy metadata.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pki/anchors
Configured certificate trust inputs. Store local CA trust here.
Inputs may be PEM certificates, trusted PEM certificates, canonical DER
certificates or .p11-kit policy files. Malformed encodings and input
symlinks are rejected before extraction.
.TP
.I /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt
Generated TLS PEM bundle.
.TP
.I /etc/ssl/certs
Generated TLS certificate files and subject-hash links.
.TP
.I /etc/ssl/certs/.p11-kit-managed
Names generated by the compatibility helper.
.TP
.I /etc/ssl/.trust-extract.*
Private staging and retained previous directories.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B sudo update-ca-trust extract
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means successful extraction or unchanged outputs. Nonzero means failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR trust (1),
.BR openssl (1)
